.TH WERKMEISTER-WORKSPACE-SERVE 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-workspace\-serve \- Serve a folder inside this workspace on 127.0.0.1 at an ephemeral port, for a browser check of a static page
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister workspace serve\fR <dir>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Runs \fBpython3 \-I \-u \-m http.server 0 \-b 127.0.0.1 \-d <dir>\fR in the foreground: loopback only, a port the OS picks (the first line prints it). Refuses a \fB<dir>\fR whose real path is outside the workspace, is the workspace folder itself, or is in a dot\-folder: those hold its daemon token and \fB.env\fR files. It resolves only \fB<dir>\fR itself, so a symlink inside it is still followed. The ICM stage contracts name it for a browser check of a static HTML page, since the Chrome tool refuses \fBfile://\fR; each ICM run pre\-approves it. Run it as a background job and stop it by its task ID.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
werkmeister workspace serve stages
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
